      </configuration_text>
      <configuration_text>
        <para>If <xref linkend="#FEAT_PMUv3_EXT32">FEAT_PMUv3_EXT32</xref> is implemented, support for 64-bit atomic reads is <arm-defined-word>IMPLEMENTATION DEFINED</arm-defined-word>. If 64-bit atomic reads are implemented, a 64-bit read of PMPCSR has the same side-effect as a 32-bit read of PMCSR[31:0] followed by a 32-bit read of PMPCSR[63:32], returning the combined value. For example, if the PE is in Debug state, then a 64-bit atomic read returns bits[31:0] == <hexnumber>0xFFFFFFFF</hexnumber> and bits[63:32] <arm-defined-word>UNKNOWN</arm-defined-word>.</para>
      </configuration_text>

      </reg_configuration>
      
      
        
